
<div class="container py-5">
  <div class="text-center mb-5">
    <h1 class="display-5 fw-bold text-success">About FoodieHub</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      A Ruby on Rails application for exploring food and drink recipes.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>Project Overview</h2>
  <p>
    FoodieHub allows visitors to explore vegetarian and
    non-vegetarian meals, discover drinks, search recipes,
    browse categories, and view ingredients and instructions.
  </p>

  <h2 class="mt-5">Our Database</h2>
  <div class="row g-3 mb-4">
    <div class="col-md-3">
      <div class="card p-3 text-center">
        <h3><%= Category.count %></h3>
        <p>Categories</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="col-md-3">
      <div class="card p-3 text-center">
        <h3><%= Recipe.count %></h3>
        <p>Recipes</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="col-md-3">
      <div class="card p-3 text-center">
        <h3><%= Ingredient.count %></h3>
        <p>Ingredients</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="col-md-3">
      <div class="card p-3 text-center">
        <h3><%= RecipeIngredient.count %></h3>
        <p>Recipe Ingredients</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>Data Sources</h2>
  <p>
    FoodieHub imports recipe information from two public APIs:
  </p>

  <ul>
    <li>
      <a href="https://www.themealdb.com/api.php"
         target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
        TheMealDB
      </a>
      — Food recipes, images, ingredients and instructions.
    </li>

    <li>
      <a href="https://www.thecocktaildb.com/api.php"
         target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
        TheCocktailDB
      </a>
      — Drink recipes, images, ingredients and instructions.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2 class="mt-5">Database Relationships</h2>
  <p>
    FoodieHub uses four ActiveRecord models:
    Category, Recipe, Ingredient and RecipeIngredient.
  </p>

  <ul>
    <li>One Category has many Recipes.</li>
    <li>Each Recipe belongs to one Category.</li>
    <li>Recipes have many Ingredients through RecipeIngredients.</li>
    <li>Ingredients can belong to many Recipes.</li>
    <li>RecipeIngredient stores the quantity of each ingredient.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 class="mt-5">Technologies</h2>
  <p>
    Ruby on Rails, SQLite, ActiveRecord, Bootstrap,
    ERB, Kaminari, Git and GitHub.
  </p>
</div>
